1
00:00:07,111 --> 00:00:11,182
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:12,450 --> 00:00:13,651
Huh.

3
00:00:13,651 --> 00:00:14,919
Wow.

4
00:00:14,919 --> 00:00:17,455
I feel like the universe doesn't
know what to do with me,

5
00:00:17,455 --> 00:00:20,692
so it's just puking me up from
one room to the next.

6
00:00:20,692 --> 00:00:23,227
I don't know where I'm getting
this imagery exactly,

7
00:00:23,227 --> 00:00:26,230
but it feels like my reward for
escaping one situation

8
00:00:26,230 --> 00:00:29,767
where I could be stranded
forever and/or killed,

9
00:00:29,767 --> 00:00:33,404
is to enter another room where I
face the exact same dilemma.

10
00:00:33,404 --> 00:00:37,875
Seriously, for what I've been through
today, the next room should contain, like,

11
00:00:37,875 --> 00:00:39,510
strippers and party balloons,

12
00:00:39,510 --> 00:00:42,213
[machine gun fire]
champagne, something along those lines.

13
00:00:42,213 --> 00:00:43,948
[machine gun fire]
See, not gunshots.

14
00:00:43,948 --> 00:00:45,350
Hey!

15
00:00:45,350 --> 00:00:50,054
You dumb shits are finally
attacking the aliens!

16
00:00:50,054 --> 00:00:52,156
That's...that's a big one.

17
00:00:52,156 --> 00:00:54,625
Y'know what, I'm just going to get out
of your way and let you do your job;

18
00:00:54,625 --> 00:00:56,427
I have total confidence in you.

19
00:00:56,427 --> 00:00:57,362
Go Army!

20
00:00:57,362 --> 00:00:59,430
Or Marines!
Or whatever you guys are.

21
00:00:59,430 --> 00:01:01,632
Not you, God dammit!

22
00:01:01,632 --> 00:01:03,634
Spontaneous alien combustion.

23
00:01:03,634 --> 00:01:04,936
Works for me.

24
00:01:06,337 --> 00:01:08,006
If I could blow people up with my mind,

25
00:01:08,006 --> 00:01:10,875
I could solve all my
problems in like one day.

26
00:01:10,875 --> 00:01:12,343
[gargantua roars]

27
00:01:13,244 --> 00:01:14,746
Okay, maybe not all my problems,

28
00:01:14,746 --> 00:01:17,548
but earthquakes were never
on the list until today.

29
00:01:17,548 --> 00:01:19,951
Whoa, that was close!

30
00:01:20,451 --> 00:01:22,954
Okay!  God!  I'll go another way!

31
00:01:23,821 --> 00:01:26,457
Hm, I don't hear any more gunshots.

32
00:01:26,457 --> 00:01:29,727
I lied.  I don't have confidence
in those soldiers.

33
00:01:29,727 --> 00:01:31,929
I mean, it took them this long
just to figure out that me

34
00:01:31,929 --> 00:01:34,932
and the other
scientists aren't the aliens.

35
00:01:34,932 --> 00:01:37,769
I've heard jokes about military
intelligence before,

36
00:01:37,769 --> 00:01:41,305
but I just thought they were exaggerations.

37
00:01:41,305 --> 00:01:43,007
Wow, that looks hot.

38
00:01:43,007 --> 00:01:44,675
I want some marshmallows.

39
00:01:44,675 --> 00:01:46,277
[vortigaunts charging up]
What the hell are YOU looking at?!

40
00:01:46,778 --> 00:01:50,648
I don't HAVE any marshmallows, and even
if I did, I wouldn't give any to you!

41
00:01:50,648 --> 00:01:51,416
THEY'RE MINE!

42
00:01:51,416 --> 00:01:52,850
EVERYTHING'S MINE!

43
00:01:52,850 --> 00:01:55,686
[gargantua roars]

44
00:01:55,686 --> 00:01:57,755
Well, this facility's not mine.

45
00:01:57,755 --> 00:02:00,024
I thought I wanted it but now I don't.

46
00:02:00,758 --> 00:02:01,926
Ah.

47
00:02:01,926 --> 00:02:05,263
See, I had a plan for how to rise
up the corporate ladder, too.

48
00:02:05,797 --> 00:02:07,198
We promote internally,

49
00:02:07,932 --> 00:02:10,868
so I was going to kidnap the
wife of the company president,

50
00:02:11,869 --> 00:02:17,141
then, as a list of demands, I'd say the
manager above me gets, I dunno, $50,000.

51
00:02:17,141 --> 00:02:18,142
Uh, hold on.

52
00:02:19,343 --> 00:02:21,512
So, then I let him sweat
it out for a few days,

53
00:02:22,413 --> 00:02:22,680
release her,

54
00:02:23,948 --> 00:02:25,383
and then, money or no money,

55
00:02:26,451 --> 00:02:27,985
the manager's finished.

56
00:02:27,985 --> 00:02:30,721
If he's not arrested, then no way
in hell's he's keeping his job

57
00:02:30,721 --> 00:02:33,157
with guilt of association like that.

58
00:02:33,157 --> 00:02:34,992
Eh, this isn't the right ammo.

59
00:02:34,992 --> 00:02:36,327
But, who am I kidding?

60
00:02:36,327 --> 00:02:38,162
This company's never going to recover.

61
00:02:38,162 --> 00:02:40,631
I wasn't looking forward to
kidnapping anyway.

62
00:02:40,631 --> 00:02:42,633
I wonder if this was
boarded up for a reason.

63
00:02:43,367 --> 00:02:46,370
[grunting]

64
00:02:47,538 --> 00:02:49,173
Heeeeeere's Johnny!

65
00:02:49,173 --> 00:02:50,675
Hey, how did you get in here?

66
00:02:51,375 --> 00:02:52,677
Are you drunk?

67
00:02:53,277 --> 00:02:53,911
Oooh...

68
00:02:53,911 --> 00:02:56,114
GUARD: Mister, if you
can get the power on,

69
00:02:56,114 --> 00:02:58,082
GUARD: that train would take ya
straight to the surface.

70
00:02:58,082 --> 00:02:59,117
Are you serious?

71
00:02:59,117 --> 00:03:00,084
GUARD: I would try it myself,

72
00:03:00,084 --> 00:03:01,085
Wha--where is it?

73
00:03:01,085 --> 00:03:03,454
GUARD: but it's a long way down
to the generator room,

74
00:03:03,454 --> 00:03:05,456
GUARD: and there are...
I want to get out of here!

75
00:03:05,456 --> 00:03:06,858
GUARD: things... in the way.

76
00:03:06,858 --> 00:03:08,392
So, does this switch do it?

77
00:03:08,392 --> 00:03:09,627
What's the procedure here?

78
00:03:09,627 --> 00:03:10,995
C'mon!  I'm ready to go!

79
00:03:11,562 --> 00:03:12,763
Come on...

80
00:03:12,763 --> 00:03:14,665
Yeah, okay, I'll take the ammo.

81
00:03:14,665 --> 00:03:17,368
Yep, that thing's still scary.

82
00:03:17,368 --> 00:03:19,437
C'mon, do any of these do anything?

83
00:03:20,404 --> 00:03:23,007
Blood...God dammit....all right.

84
00:03:23,007 --> 00:03:25,042
That thing has flamethrowers, doesn't it?

85
00:03:25,042 --> 00:03:26,944
Why does it have flamethrowers?

86
00:03:26,944 --> 00:03:30,114
Jesus Christ, I think that IS
a punch card slot.

87
00:03:30,114 --> 00:03:33,484
Eh, I'm getting out of here;
that monster's scaring me,

88
00:03:33,484 --> 00:03:36,854
and, uh, you...have your gun if
it gives you any trouble,

89
00:03:36,854 --> 00:03:38,756
so, we're cool.

90
00:03:38,756 --> 00:03:39,857
Later!

91
00:03:39,857 --> 00:03:41,058
Take it easy.

92
00:03:41,058 --> 00:03:44,128
Okay, I think he said that the
train needs power.

93
00:03:44,128 --> 00:03:45,229
Power.

94
00:03:45,229 --> 00:03:46,697
I need power.

95
00:03:46,697 --> 00:03:48,699
I have the power to get the power.

96
00:03:48,699 --> 00:03:50,801
Because...huh...

97
00:03:50,801 --> 00:03:53,037
These things would
make cool lawn ornaments.

98
00:03:53,037 --> 00:03:54,872
I wonder if I could find a
taxidermist that would--

99
00:03:54,872 --> 00:03:57,141
[gargantua roars]

100
00:03:57,141 --> 00:03:58,176
Rumble rubble...

101
00:03:58,176 --> 00:03:59,243
rubble rumble.

102
00:03:59,243 --> 00:04:00,878
Rubble rumble, rubble rumble.

103
00:04:00,878 --> 00:04:02,280
[vortiguant charges up]
No, dammit!

104
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:04,182
I'm not calling you!

105
00:04:04,182 --> 00:04:04,815
What?

106
00:04:05,349 --> 00:04:07,818
Where did that come from?
It fell from the ceiling.

107
00:04:07,818 --> 00:04:09,353
Oh.

108
00:04:09,353 --> 00:04:11,789
Boy, you could stash some drugs in there.

109
00:04:11,789 --> 00:04:14,091
Mm, I don't see any.
Maybe the aliens ate them.

110
00:04:15,193 --> 00:04:16,227
Alien sale!

111
00:04:17,361 --> 00:04:18,529
Prices are falling.

112
00:04:19,997 --> 00:04:24,001
No, wait.  It's the aliens that
are falling.  The prices are--

113
00:04:24,001 --> 00:04:26,170
No, I'm not sure that works.

114
00:04:26,170 --> 00:04:30,808
Hmm.  Yeah, I think I could talk a
taxidermist into stuffing one of these.

115
00:04:30,808 --> 00:04:32,476
Just tell them I don't know what it is.

116
00:04:32,476 --> 00:04:33,744
I found it hunting.

117
00:04:33,744 --> 00:04:36,380
I think it might be a weird kind of rabbit.

118
00:04:36,380 --> 00:04:38,182
He might buy it.  I dunno.

119
00:04:38,182 --> 00:04:39,650
I'm a good liar.

120
00:04:39,650 --> 00:04:40,384
[vortigaunts charging up]
Shut up!

121
00:04:40,384 --> 00:04:42,153
[explosion]
I don't want your opinion.

122
00:04:42,954 --> 00:04:44,956
I wouldn't even be lying, really.

123
00:04:44,956 --> 00:04:47,291
Because this is...sort of like hunting.

124
00:04:47,291 --> 00:04:50,027
And I really don't know
what these things are.

125
00:04:50,027 --> 00:04:53,297
Though I do know that they're not
rabbits.  I'd have to lie about that.

126
00:04:54,865 --> 00:04:57,134
Oh. "894GH".

127
00:04:57,134 --> 00:05:00,438
That tells me where I am about
as much as I already know.

128
00:05:01,505 --> 00:05:06,310
Ah.  Y'know, I think these doors
ARE sealed for a reason.

129
00:05:06,310 --> 00:05:07,878
Oh boy.  Yeah.

130
00:05:07,878 --> 00:05:09,513
God, not on my suit!

131
00:05:09,513 --> 00:05:12,683
I just plunged into water at
almost terminal velocity!

132
00:05:12,683 --> 00:05:15,319
I don't need it getting
messed up again!

133
00:05:15,319 --> 00:05:18,589
I'm still not crazy about the orange
color, but it's a good suit.

134
00:05:18,589 --> 00:05:20,424
Oh, are these grenade rounds?

135
00:05:20,424 --> 00:05:22,593
[gunshots]
What the fuck?!

136
00:05:22,593 --> 00:05:25,730
FOR THE UMPTEENTH TIME,
I'M NOT AN ALIEN!

137
00:05:27,865 --> 00:05:29,867
Un-fucking-believable.

138
00:05:29,867 --> 00:05:32,803
And here I thought they
finally figured that out.

139
00:05:32,803 --> 00:05:35,973
That's what I get for giving
people ANY credit.

140
00:05:35,973 --> 00:05:39,610
I saw them shooting the aliens
and not me for once,

141
00:05:39,610 --> 00:05:44,148
and I ASSUMED that the military finally
got it through their thick-ass skulls

142
00:05:44,148 --> 00:05:46,617
which targets they're
supposed to shoot at!

143
00:05:46,617 --> 00:05:48,352
But, no, no, no, no...

144
00:05:48,352 --> 00:05:50,821
That's for smart people like me.

145
00:05:50,821 --> 00:05:56,093
I know it's obvious I'm a genius,
but is everyone else really this stupid?

146
00:05:56,093 --> 00:05:59,430
I don't know, but I do know how to
prove who's more dead between us.

147
00:05:59,430 --> 00:06:00,197
[whistling sound]

148
00:06:00,197 --> 00:06:02,366
[turret firing]
Ah ah, ah, ah!

149
00:06:02,366 --> 00:06:03,534
[turret beeping]
Why?

150
00:06:03,534 --> 00:06:04,635
[turret beeping]
No, not my suit!

151
00:06:04,635 --> 00:06:05,303
[turret beeping]

152
00:06:05,303 --> 00:06:07,538
[turret beeping]
THE SUIT DENTS WHEN YOU SHOOT
IT,

153
00:06:07,538 --> 00:06:09,940
[turret beeping]
SO STOP SHOOTING IT!

154
00:06:09,940 --> 00:06:12,576
[turret beeping]
I hate you all so much...

155
00:06:12,576 --> 00:06:15,646
[turret beeping]

156
00:06:15,646 --> 00:06:18,115
[turret beeping]
Well, I guess I'll wait 
for this to die down...

157
00:06:18,115 --> 00:06:19,650
[turret beeping]

158
00:06:19,650 --> 00:06:21,285
[turret beeping]
Yep...

159
00:06:21,285 --> 00:06:23,285
[turret beeping]

